## Fast markets and stop losses

When a build returns `reason: "presign_refused"` and `retryable: true`, rebuild immediately for a
fresh quote. Nothing was signed or broadcast. You can reuse the same `clientTradeId` for an
unchanged request or use a new one. Use a new ID if you change the request. If the response sets
`retryable: false`, resolve the reported cause before rebuilding.

For stop-loss sells on fast-moving tokens, pass a wider `maxSlippageBps` on the build if you can
accept a lower minimum output. The default is 100 bps (1%) and the cap is 5,000 bps (50%). A Jupiter
slippage refusal (error 6001) can be identified by `cause: "slippage_exceeded"` in the API response.
The TypeScript SDK exposes `refusal` and `detail` on `CandleApiError`.

In Node.js, pass `fetch: fastConnectFetch(apiUrl)` to `CandleClient`. This example gives API reads and
trade builds a 3-second connection timeout and retries once immediately on `UND_ERR_CONNECT_TIMEOUT`.
The retry sends the same request body and `clientTradeId`. If a submit or confirm times out, look up
the trade's status before deciding what to do.

```ts
import { Agent, fetch as undiciFetch, type RequestInit } from "undici"

function fastConnectFetch(apiUrl: string): typeof fetch {
  const origin = new URL(apiUrl).origin
  const dispatcher = new Agent({ connect: { timeout: 3_000 } })

  return async (input, init) => {
    if (typeof input !== "string") return fetch(input, init)
    const url = new URL(input)
    const method = (init?.method ?? "GET").toUpperCase()
    const isRead = method === "GET" || method === "HEAD"
    const isBuild = method === "POST" && url.pathname === "/api/v1/trade/agent/build"
    if (url.origin !== origin || !(isRead || isBuild)) return fetch(input, init)

    const options: RequestInit = { ...(init as RequestInit), dispatcher, redirect: "manual" }
    const send = () => undiciFetch(input, options) as unknown as Promise<Response>
    try {
      return await send()
    } catch (error) {
      const code = (error as { cause?: { code?: string } }).cause?.code
      if (code !== "UND_ERR_CONNECT_TIMEOUT") throw error
      return await send()
    }
  }
}
```
